        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/qdrant/qdrant/pulls/10128",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/10128",
          "diff_url": "https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/10128.diff",
          "patch_url": "https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/10128.patch",
          "merged_at": "2026-08-08T15:54:55Z"
        },
        "body": "## Summary\n- Remove the arbitrary NullIndex heuristic `exp = 2/3 * estimated` (\"assuming 1/3 of the points are deleted\") for `is_empty=true` and `is_null=false`.\n- Use the indexed upper bound (`total_point_count − has_values` / `− is_null`) as `exp` instead, which matches exact counts when there are no soft-deletes.\n- Fixes the ~35% systematic under-count reported in #10120 for `count` with `exact=false` on `is_empty`.\n\n## Context\nNullIndex already knows the complement size; higher layers do not further correct for soft-deletes on the approx-count path. The 1/3 discount was introduced ad hoc in #6504 and caused biased approx counts at steady state.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `cargo test -p segment --lib index::field_index::null_index`\n- [ ] Reproduce #10120 script: `is_empty` approx count should match exact when there are no deletes\n- [ ] Spot-check `is_null=false` approx count similarly",
        "reactions": {
