        },
        "body": "## Summary\n- Re-introduces the NullIndex cardinality change from #10128 after its revert (#10140).\n- #10128 was merged without GitHub Actions rust-tests; post-merge `dev` CI failed on `payload_index_test::test_read_operations` / `test_is_empty_conditions` (`468.0 vs 227.0` at line 696).\n- Branch rebuilt on current `dev` (after squash-merge of #10140) so the PR diff is non-empty and CI can exercise the change.\n\n## Context\nNullIndex used `exp = 2/3 * estimated` for complement conditions (`is_empty=true`, `is_null=false`). This removes that discount and uses the indexed upper bound as `exp` (see #10120).\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] Expect `rust-tests` to fail on `segment::integration::payload_index_test::test_read_operations`\n- [ ] Fix estimation and/or relax the integration assertion, then re-run CI",
